        "original_id": "2a37efb4-940d-5324-b7cd-90ce2d5e4b14",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kay Pollak, Chester Erskine, Thomas Fryk, Ingvar Hirdwall\n- Films: Children's Island, A Girl in Every Port\n- Roles: film director, writer, producer\n- Places: Sweden, Hollywood, Broadway\n\nFacts:\n- Chester Erskine was born on November 29, 1905, and he was a Hollywood and Broadway director, writer, and producer.\n- Kay Gunnar Leopold Pollak was born on May 21, 1938, and he is a Swedish film director.\n- A Girl in Every Port is a 1952 comedy film directed by Chester Erskine.\n- Children's Island, also titled Barnens ö in Swedish, is a Swedish drama film that was released in Sweden on December 25, 1980.\n- Children's Island was directed by Kay Pollak and starred Thomas Fryk and Ingvar Hirdwall.\n- Chester Erskine died on April 7, 1986.",
